---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Field from '../../components/Field.astro';
import { link } from '../../lib/links';
---

<Shell
  property="cloud"
  title="Guild Cloud — The Guild Inference Project"
  description="Guild Cloud is the planned hosted inference platform from The Guild Inference Project, built on the systems work behind Guild. In development; no public endpoints or pricing are available."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="dot"></span> The Guild Inference Project // Cloud (in development)
      </div>
      <h1>Beyond your<br /><em>own machine.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Local inference puts you in control. Hosted inference should make it easier to get started.
        Guild Cloud is The Guild Inference Project’s planned platform for bringing Guild’s systems
        approach to a managed environment.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#direction">
          Our direction <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={link('docs', 'serving/')}>
          Self-host Guild today <span>↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Field variant="cloud" />
  </section>

  <section id="direction" class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-label">01 / Product direction</span>
      <h2>Less infrastructure<br />between you and an idea.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <span>
        Your Machine
        <small>Guild local runtime · available today</small>
      </span>
      <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
      <span>
        Shared Contracts
        <small>GPACK containers & local API</small>
      </span>
      <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
      <span>
        Guild Cloud
        <small>Managed platform · in development</small>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars">
      <article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">01</span>
        <h3>A familiar interface</h3>
        <p>
          We intend to build on Guild’s existing local API capabilities, making integration with
          applications a central design goal.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">02</span>
        <h3>Hardware-aware execution</h3>
        <p>
          The starting point is Guild’s work on heterogeneous memory, portable model packages, and
          machine-specific optimization.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar">
        <span class="number">03</span>
        <h3>Visible boundaries</h3>
        <p>
          Model compatibility, resource limits, and measured performance should be clear before you
          depend on a service.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="statement">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">02 / Where things stand</span>
        <h2>Building the foundation.<br /><em>Not yet a service.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Our hosted cloud platform is in development. Public inference endpoints, API keys,
          pricing, launch dates, and service-level commitments are not available yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          For inference you can run today, Guild is open source. Build the engine, choose a
          compatible model, and serve it on your own hardware.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={link('docs', 'serving/')}>
          Read the self-hosting guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Guild inference engine <span>Available source</span></li>
          <li>Local API serving <span>Available in Guild</span></li>
          <li>Managed hosted inference <span>In development</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Shell>
